
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.DetectedTouchPos(Index: number): vector`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector llDetectedTouchPos(integer Index);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns the vector position where the object was touched in <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Viewer_coordinate_frames#Region" target="_blank">region coordinates</a>, unless it is <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetAttached" target="_blank">attached</a> to the HUD, in which case it returns the position in screen space coordinates.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>integer</span></td>
          <td>Index / <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Parameters/index" target="_blank">index</a></td>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>It's 1 based</span>Index of detection information</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>detected</li>
        <li>touch</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">339</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
        <span class="attr-label bg-detected">Detected Event</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p><b>index</b> <i>does not</i> support <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Negative_Index" target="_blank">negative indexes</a>.</p>
  <p>For the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Touch" target="_blank">touch</a> category of events only. The prim that was touched may not be the prim receiving the event, use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDetectedLinkNumber" target="_blank">llDetectedLinkNumber</a> to check for this; likewise you can use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDetectedTouchFace" target="_blank">llDetectedTouchFace</a> to determine which face was touched.</p>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>HUD attachments currently return coordinates relative to the <i>center of the screen</i> rather than the attachment point. <a href="https://jira.secondlife.com/browse/SVC-3425" target="_blank">SVC-3425</a></li>
    <li>If <b>index</b> is out of bounds the script continues to execute without an error message.</li>
    <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/TOUCH_INVALID_VECTOR" target="_blank">TOUCH_INVALID_VECTOR</a> is returned when...
    <ul>
      <li>The avatar&#39;s viewer does not support face touch detection.
      <ul>
        <li>To check if face touch detection is supported check the return of <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDetectedTouchFace" target="_blank">llDetectedTouchFace</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    
      </li>
      <li>The touch has moved off the surface of the prim.</li>
      <li>The event triggered is not a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Touch" target="_blank">touch</a> event.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num_detected = #events
    ll.Whisper(0, "Pos clicked: " .. tostring(ll.DetectedTouchPos(0)))
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    touch_start(integer num_detected)
    {
        llWhisper(0, "Pos clicked: " + (string)llDetectedTouchPos(0));
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function GetRealTouchPos(pos)
    --  By Ariu Arai for free use to anyone
    --  Returns a useful HUD Position Vector from the llDetectedTouchPos(); function
    --  USE: vector pos = GetRealTouchPos(llDetectedTouchPos(0)); .. Etc.
    --  This function is intended to be used to move child prims to where the user clicks. This does not work on the root prim.

    local point = ll.GetAttached()
    local offset = ZERO_VECTOR

    if point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_RIGHT then
        offset = vector(1.0, 0.933, -0.5)
    elseif point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_CENTER then
        offset = vector(1.0, 0.000, -0.5)
    elseif point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_LEFT then
        offset = vector(1.0, -0.933, -0.5)
    elseif point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM_LEFT then
        offset = vector(1.0, -0.933, 0.5)
    elseif point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM then
        offset = vector(1.0, 0.000, 0.5)
    elseif point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM_RIGHT then
        offset = vector(1.0, 0.933, 0.5)
    end

    --return (pos - llGetLocalPos()) + (offset * llGetLocalRot());
    return ((offset - ll.GetLocalPos()) + pos) / ll.GetLocalRot()
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector GetRealTouchPos(vector pos)
{
//  By Ariu Arai for free use to anyone
//  Returns a useful HUD Position Vector from the llDetectedTouchPos(); function
//  USE: vector pos = GetRealTouchPos(llDetectedTouchPos(0)); .. Etc.
//  This function is intended to be used to move child prims to where the user clicks. This does not work on the root prim.

    integer point = llGetAttached();
    vector offset;

    if      (point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_RIGHT)    offset = <1.0, 0.933,-0.5>;
    else if (point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_CENTER)   offset = <1.0, 0.000,-0.5>;
    else if (point == ATTACH_HUD_TOP_LEFT)     offset = <1.0,-0.933,-0.5>;
    else if (point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM_LEFT)  offset = <1.0,-0.933, 0.5>;
    else if (point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM)       offset = <1.0, 0.000, 0.5>;
    else if (point == ATTACH_HUD_BOTTOM_RIGHT) offset = <1.0, 0.933, 0.5>;

    //return (pos - llGetLocalPos()) + (offset * llGetLocalRot());
    return ((offset - llGetLocalPos()) + pos) / llGetLocalRot();
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
